<title>USA: U.S. July housing starts unchanged.</title>
<headline>U.S. July housing starts unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce housing starts and building permits, seasonally adjusted annual rates, in 1,000s:</p>
<p> PCT CHANGE:July    June (Prev)     May (Prev)  July97/96</p>
<p> -Starts    Unch     3.2    4.8    -5.5   -6.6	 -3.0</p>
<p> -Permits    1.4    -2.1   -2.6    -0.7   -0.7	 -2.2</p>
<p> RATES	July    June (Prev)     May (Prev)  July 1996</p>
<p> -Starts   1,447   1,447  1,452   1,402  1,385	1,492</p>
<p> -Permits  1,422   1,402  1,395   1,432  1,432	1,454</p>
<p> STARTS:    July    June (Prev)     May (Prev)  July 1996</p>
<p> -Single   1,141   1,111  1,110   1,098  1,082	1,164</p>
<p> -Multiple   306     336    342     304    303	  328</p>
<p> PERMITS    July    June (Prev)     May (Prev)  July 1996</p>
<p> -Single   1,029   1,049  1,045   1,053  1,053	1,077</p>
<p> -Multiple   393     353    350     379    379	  377</p>
<p>  JULY STARTS--Pct--Rate    JULY PERMITS-Pct---Rate</p>
<p> -NorthEast   41.4   157    -Northeast   5.9   143</p>
<p> -Midwest     -3.7   289    -Midwest    -7.1   275</p>
<p> -South	 -2.4   663    -South	 1.9   653</p>
<p> -West	  -5.3   338    -West	  6.4   351</p>
<p>Actual Starts and Permits, unadjusted in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -	 July  June   May July96</p>
<p>  Starts     133   133   136   138</p>
<p>  Permits    133   132   132   135</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast July starts at a 1.46 million unit annual rate.</p>
<p>The Commerce Department said Northeast starts for July were at their highest rate since November 1994, when they rose 41.9 percent.  </p>
<p>Permits for the Midwest in July were at their lowest level since March 1995, when they measured 274,000. Permits for South were at their highest level since May 1996, when they totalled 662,000.</p>
